sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/delphisci-swarm-04-published-delphi-templates-use-legacy-probknow-iris> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The published \"Project Delphi claim\" and \"Project Delphi evidence item\" templates (2026-10-23) state their statements with legacy probknow (pk:) IRIs, while the delphi skill requires Delphi ontology v2.0 terms and says probknow IRIs are never used in new records, so a record written to the skill fails template conformance." ;
    dct:description "Template https://w3id.org/np/RAI0QFH7bCNJIeKxwG3EbX5QKyoOjlaESiJkVZKs8iUc8 (\"Project Delphi claim\", created 2026-10-23T13:08:44Z, creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1267-0234) declares @prefix pk: <https://w3id.org/probknow/ontology/> and uses pk: terms 11 times (Claim, context, derivedFromPaper, hasAssessment, weightOfEvidence); it uses no https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/ IRI. Template https://w3id.org/np/RAG7UB06LpEpmDKX8VFoIbeTwyRg5m9vnadwKwTuahwes (\"Project Delphi evidence item\", created 2026-10-23T13:08:44Z, creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1267-0234) uses pk: terms 13 times (EvidenceItem, derivedFromPaper, pValue, statisticalTest, vovkSellkeMaxPRatio, weightOfEvidence), again with no delphi: IRI. Both were fetched from w3id.org with Accept: application/trig on 2026-10-31 and are kept verbatim under swarm/nanopubs/evidence. The delphi skill (https://github.com/knowledgepixels/project-delphi-nanopubs/blob/6c543f4698ca1275247e370cc4c51cb9e09eab12/skills/delphi/SKILL.md, line 26) says: \"The legacy `https://w3id.org/probknow/...` IRIs are never used in new records.\" and that terms come from Delphi ontology v2.0 with prefix delphi: = https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/. The nanopub skill's check-nanopub-conformance.py therefore reports every delphi: triple as unmatched and the template's required statement st01 (rdf:type pk:Claim or pk:EvidenceItem) as not instantiated, for this repository's records and for its earlier math-bio-theorems drafts alike." ;
    delphi:context "Checked while drafting Delphi records for the swarm comparison on 2026-10-31, with nanopub-java 1.95.0 and the nanopub skill's conformance script. The skill revision read is commit 6c543f46 of knowledgepixels/project-delphi-nanopubs (2026-10-26)." ;
    skos:note "Status: supported (direct observation of the served templates and the skill text on 2026-10-31). Decision taken by the DELPHI hub on 2026-10-31 and recorded in swarm/nanopubs/DECISIONS.md: follow the skill, write delphi: v2.0 terms, and do not declare nt:wasCreatedFromTemplate for a template whose placeholders the record cannot fill (that triple would assert a false provenance); instead name the template that would otherwise apply, its pk: count and the date checked in an rdfs:comment. Reported so other teams do not lose time rediscovering it." ;
    skos:scopeNote "What this does not establish. (1) It does not say which side should change: the ontology's own crosswalk maps the probknow terms to delphi: terms, so the templates may be updated or the skill relaxed. (2) Only these two templates were checked; the other Project Delphi templates of the same date (assessments, rubric, testable hypothesis) were not inspected. (3) Templates are versioned (dct:isVersionOf …/claimKind and …/evidenceKind); a later governed version may already resolve this by the time anyone reads this record. (4) The counts are occurrences of pk: tokens in the TriG serialization as served on 2026-10-31, not a semantic count." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/delphisci-swarm-04-published-delphi-templates-use-legacy-probknow-iris> .
}

